From 6685b636a9d026d834c3d63b9184891526e1565d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 07:11:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Declare ucode helpers before their first caller (#62, #87,
 #115)

Declare ucode helpers before their first caller

ucode resolves identifiers when a file is compiled, so a top-level
function called before its declaration is looked up as a global and
fails at runtime with "left-hand side is not a function" (#62, #115).

Move the remaining helpers above their first caller:
- components/action.uc: updates_log/log_message (used by the tmpfs
  space guard, so a low-space install crashed instead of logging)
- server/service.uc: safe_filename_string (TLS defaults)
- service/initd.uc: release_runtime_dir_lock, owner_pid_value
- service/state.uc: release_runtime_dir_lock
- service/ui.uc: release_dir_lock

These paths only run on lock contention, low tmpfs space or TLS setup
without certificates, so the test suite did not reach them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HEQfjBzS7Wos7AvTk18TDQ
